25.steps:
1) Go to Network>Interface page and choose IPv6 radio button in View IP Version IPv4 IPv6.
2)Open configuration page of an interface, say X1, X1 WAN IPv6 auto mode;
3)Enable HTTPS management, test HTTPS management via this auto IPv6 address;
4)Change IPv6 mode from auto to static, test step 3 again;  5)Change IPv6 mode to DHCPv6, test step 3 again;
6)Disable HTTPS management.

36.steps:
1) Configure a WAN interface X1, it is the default WAN, and set its IPv6 ip-assignment as static, configure 4600::1 as static gateway, enable listen to RA, but do not connect it to router right now.
2)Check routing table, there will be a default route, use 4600::1 as gateway,and X1 is the output interface, metric is 20, check packets int FW, no RA received by now; 
3)Connect it to a router, enable RA, check packets in FW, it received RA from router; 
4)On IPv6 address part, verify display of added additional static IPv6 address.
4)Check routing table, it will generated another default route learned from RA, metric is 50, check its gateway, it should be RA message's source IP.
